{"name":"Golden","hex":"#f5bf03","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Golden","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname.","A female given name."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Ellipsis of Golden Retriever."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Golden"}],"entries":[{"title":"Probus, Cornwall","blocks":[{"text":"Probus is a civil parish and village in Cornwall, England, in the United Kingdom. It has the tallest church tower in Cornwall. The tower is 129 feet (39 m) high, and richly decorated with carvings. The place name originates from the church's dedication to an obscure Saint Probus. The parish population at the 2011 census was 2,299, whereas the ward population taken at the same census was 3,953."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Probus_st_probus_and_st_grace_001.jpg/330px-Probus_st_probus_and_st_grace_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Probus%2C_Cornwall"},{"title":"Golden Cap","blocks":[{"text":"Golden Cap is a hill and cliff situated on the English Channel coast between Bridport and Charmouth in Dorset, England. At 191 metres (627 ft), it is the highest point within a mile of the south coast of Great Britain and is visible for tens of miles along the coastline. It is accessible via a coastal footpath from Seatown, and takes around 40 minutes to reach the summit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Golden_Cap_from_Charmouth_beach.jpg/330px-Golden_Cap_from_Charmouth_beach.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Cap"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campai